ns towards the end and  I have now decided I'm not gonna spoil  it but with some of the things you  realize towards the end with what's  going on it really felt like it was  pushing it and like if I were gonna  nitpick just slightly some of these sort  of climactic stuff there's there's  extended series of characters kind of  just having speeches for lack of a  better term I think that goes on a  little too long both for individual  speeches and that section but it still  pays off really well and it feels earned  and like there's God there's honestly  this video could end up going on forever  there are so many great characters in  this the entire squad is terrific  the officers are great there are one-off  small characters that are excellent  there it's but again like despite being  this thick and super you and you having  a lot of characters and and a lot and a  lot going on in the world the narrative  is pretty straightforward join the army  fight the enemy here's the specific goal  that they have right now let's see that  if they can do that and that's basically  it so there is a lot going on but built  around a very sound  simple structure and through all that  it's just a really good book I've had  people telling me I should read Terry  Pratchett for years and I wish I could  say that this means I'll start reading a  bunch Terry Pratchett but like this took  me a while I wanted to have I was  commissioned for this review a couple  months ago and I don't like to take that  long to get to commissioned reviews but  it's hard for me to find the time to  read but I'm really glad I did this was  good and this was fun and this was funny  and and and I can vouch for the fact  that as someone who's never read the  Discworld book before my life still good  you don't need to have read the other  stuff if you know fantasy tropes at all  even a little bit you can roll with this  it's real easy so that's the monstrous  regiment first time I read Terry  Pratchett I got a I go